{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"type":"noauth"},{"scopes":["govinbox:read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Not affiliated with the U.S. government, GSA, or SAM.gov. Not a U.S. government service. Justification & Approval (J&A) notices from SAM.gov, the documents agencies publish to justify non-competitive awards. Under FAR 6.305, most J&As post 14 days AFTER award (30 days for urgency) - brand-name justifications may post with the solicitation instead (FAR 6.305(c)) - so these are usually post-decision records, not pipeline leads - the protest clock may have already run. Shows who received sole-source work, the FAR authority cited (e.g. 6.302-1 only one source, 6.302-2 urgency), the contract value, period of performance, and whether it is a bridge contract. Filter by keyword, agency, vendor name, NAICS code, or FAR authority. Vendor names and values are parsed from notice text and may be incomplete. Empty results do not mean competitive - below-threshold and exempt actions never post. Present as information only; verify every fact against the official J&A on SAM.gov before acting. One search counts as one use, regardless of how many records are returned. Every record carries a direct source link (or source name and record ID) so you can verify and cite the underlying record.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"agency":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Agency substring filter, e.g. 'DEFENSE' or 'VA'","title":"Agency"},"authority":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":16,"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"FAR authority filter, e.g. '6.302-1' or '8.405-6'","title":"Authority"},"bridge_only":{"default":false,"description":"When true, return only bridge contracts/extensions","title":"Bridge Only","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"default":20,"maximum":50,"minimum":1,"title":"Limit"